description:
Repo: genetics-results-suite. File: k8s/deployments/auth-gateway.yaml.

Today only 'location = /mcp' proxies to mcp-server; everything else under 'location /' sits behind oauth2-proxy auth_request. The discovery URL lives at the site ROOT (https://genegenie.broadinstitute.org/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource), so without a rule it would hit the frontend behind oauth2-proxy and never reach mcp-server. Add exact-match locations that proxy to mcp-server WITHOUT auth_request:
  location = /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource { proxy_pass .../.well-known/oauth-protected-resource; ... }
  location = /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp { ... }
Mirror the proxy_set_header/timeouts used by the /mcp block. Do NOT route /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server here — that's served by Keycloak on auth.<domain>. Verify with: curl -s https://genegenie.broadinstitute.org/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource returns the metadata JSON with HTTP 200 and no login redirect.

Depends on the mcp-server discovery subtask (so there's something to proxy to).
